# SecureSure Insurance — Project Charter

## 1. Project Overview

**Project name:** SecureSure Insurance — ISO 27001 GRC Implementation

**Project type:** Simulated GRC implementation and portfolio project

**Platform:** ServiceNow Personal Developer Instance (PDI), subject to available applications and permissions

**Framework:** ISO/IEC 27001:2022

## 2. Business Scenario

SecureSure Insurance is a fictional insurance company providing health and motor insurance services. The organization processes customer personal information, policy records, claims documentation and payment-related information.

The scenario will be used to demonstrate how information security governance and risk management can be implemented in an insurance environment.

## 3. Project Objectives

- Define an appropriate Information Security Management System (ISMS) scope.
- Develop an Information Security Policy and supporting policies.
- Identify information assets and assess information security risks.
- Map applicable ISO 27001 requirements to controls.
- Demonstrate control assessments, attestations and evidence collection.
- Simulate findings, corrective actions and control retesting.
- Document the implementation in ServiceNow where supported by the PDI.

## 4. Proposed Scope

The initial scope is proposed to include the customer portal, policy administration process, claims management process, employee access, corporate endpoints and supporting cloud services.

The final scope and exclusions will be documented after analyzing organizational context, dependencies and relevant interested parties.

## 5. Expected Deliverables

- Project charter and ISMS scope
- Information Security Policy and supporting policies
- Asset inventory and risk register
- ISO 27001 control mapping and Statement of Applicability
- Control assessments and simulated attestations
- Evidence, findings and remediation records
- ServiceNow configuration notes and screenshots
- Final project report and GitHub walkthrough

## 6. Assumptions and Limitations

SecureSure Insurance is fictional. All users, assets, risks, assessment results and evidence are simulated.

ServiceNow implementation depends on the applications, features and permissions available in the developer instance.

This portfolio demonstrates practical learning and does not establish certification or compliance for a real organization.

## 7. Success Criteria

Demonstrate at least one traceable scenario connecting a business asset and information security risk to applicable requirements, a defined control, an assessment supported by evidence, and a remediation or closure decision.

